Subject: vsock: non-blocking Unix proxy TX to prevent EventManager deadlocks

UnixProxy previously switched connected sockets to blocking mode and called
blocking send() directly from the VMM EventManager thread while holding
queue_tx and proxy_map.read(). When a host client paused reading from one
guest->host stream (for example, `docker export | docker run -i` when the
receiving stream hit vsock credit backpressure), send() blocked EventManager
forever: VSOCK_OP_CREDIT_UPDATE packets could never be drained from queue_tx,
new connections wedged MuxerThread on proxy_map.write(), and the control
channel stopped answering.

Keep UnixProxy sockets non-blocking, buffer unwritten guest->host bytes in a
per-connection tx_buf drained on EventSet::OUT by MuxerThread, advance tx_cnt
only as bytes are accepted by the host kernel so vsock credit throttles each
connection independently, defer guest SHUTDOWN_SEND until tx_buf empties,
handle incoming VSOCK_OP_CREDIT_REQUEST, carry fwd_cnt on MuxerRx::Shutdown,
serialize epoll/kqueue updates under each proxy's lock, signal the RX queue
when pushing CreditRequest, and delete kqueue filters individually on macOS
so ENOENT on EVFILT_READ cannot skip deleting EVFILT_WRITE.

